  "text": "积累 Step-by-step Calculation\n\n### Step 1: Define the Terms of the Geometric Progression\nWe know that in a geometric progression, each term is the product of the previous term and the common ratio \\( r \\).\n\nLet the terms of the progression be:\n- \\( a_2 = 18 \\)\n- \\( a_3 = 36 \\)\n- \\( a_4 = 54 \\)\n\n### Step 2: Express the Terms Using the Common Ratio\nUsing the definition of a geometric progression:\n\\[\na_2 = a_1 \\cdot r\n\\]\n\\[\na_3 = a_2 \\cdot r = a_1 \\cdot r^2\n\\]\n\\[\na_4 = a_3 \\cdot r = a_1 \\cdot r^3\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Set Up Equations Using the Given Terms\nFrom Step 1 and Step 2:\n\\[\na_1 \\cdot r = 18 \\quad (1)\n\\]\n\\[\na_1 \\cdot r^2 = 36 \\quad (2)\n\\]\n\\[\na_1 \\cdot r^3 = 54 \\quad (3)\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Solve for the Common Ratio \\( r \\)\nDivide equation (2) by equation (1) to eliminate \\( a_1 \\):\n\\[\n\\frac{a_1 \\cdot r^2}{a_1 \\cdot r} = \\frac{36}{18}\n\\]\n\\[\nr = 2\n\\]\n\n### Step 5: Verify the Common Ratio\nSubstitute \\( r = 2 \\) back into equation (1) to find \\( a_1 \\):\n\\[\na_1 \\cdot 2 = 18\n\\]\n\\[\na_1 = 9\n\\]\n\n### Step 6: Check the Third Term\nUsing \\( a_1 = 9 \\) and \\( r = 2 \\):\n\\[\na_3 = a_1 \\cdot r^2 = 9 \\cdot 4 = 36\n\\]\nThis matches the given term, confirming \\( r = 2 \\).\n\n### Final Answer\nThe common ratio of the progression is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]",
